Dashboard looker_holistics_validation {
  title: 'Looker Holistics Validation'
  description: 'Validation of the attention dataset against Looker. Tab 1: Direct campaign 10605 (baseline campaign 5.1997 / network 5.2332). Tab 2: six Programmatic ad ids selected together.'
  owner: 'ganonuevo@verticalcity.com'

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Controls. Both are sourced from the attention_base.report_filter PARAM (a param-sourced
  // control is the only way a value reaches a {% filter %} in the model SQL). Tab 1 takes one
  // value, tab 2 takes several. Each control is wired only to the blocks of its own tab.
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  block f_report: FilterBlock {
    label: 'Campaign ID or Ad ID (single)'
    type: 'field'
    source: FieldFilterSource {
      dataset: attention
      field: r(attention_base.report_filter)
    }
    default {
      operator: 'is'
      value: '10605'
    }
    settings {
      input_type: 'single'
    }
  }

  block f_ads: FilterBlock {
    label: 'Ad IDs (multiple)'
    type: 'field'
    source: FieldFilterSource {
      dataset: attention
      field: r(attention_base.report_filter)
    }
    default {
      operator: 'is'
      value: [
        '69d6b7f1dd289cab8bbe075a',
        '69d6b809dd289cab8bbe075f',
        '6a03890a61b5f9ea1e4f40a6',
        '6a03890a61b5f9ea1e4f40a7',
        '6a03890a61b5f9ea1e4f40a8',
        '6a03890a61b5f9ea1e4f40a9'
      ]
    }
    settings {
      input_type: 'multiple'
    }
  }

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Explanations
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  block t_intro: TextBlock {
    content: @md
## How this dataset works

1. **One control, one param.** The control writes `attention_base.report_filter` (a campaign id for Direct, an ad id for Programmatic). Inside `attention_base` the param selects the matching rows of `stg_campaigns`, takes their min/max flight dates, expands them to one row per date and **inner-joins them on `DATE(start_at_utc)`** directly on the partitioned table. Rows outside the window never leave the model (`is_in_flight_range` is true for every surviving row).
2. **Network scope.** Every block carries the AQL condition `filter_model.report_filter == coalesce(param | first(), '__all__') or ... == '__all__'` (tab 2 uses `in`). It filters `filter_model`, and the filter flows `filter_model -> stg_campaigns -> campaign_network_scope_bridge_v2 -> network_scope_v2 -> attention_base`: all events in the same cities and grouped ad lengths as the selection, from any campaign. With the control empty the sentinel keeps every row.
3. **Campaign vs network.** `average_attention_seconds` / `attention_events` are the network (campaign identity excluded from the grain, filter kept). `campaign_average_attention_seconds` / `campaign_datapoints` activate the inactive relationship `attention_base.ad_id > stg_campaigns.ad_id` with `with_relationships()` so only the selection's own events count.
4. **Comparisons.** `attention_vs_campaign` = row attention vs the whole selection (`of_all(attention_base)`); `attention_vs_network` = row attention vs the single-number network average (Looker `attention_network_average`). The gender / age / gender x age variants pin the network average to that demographic with `keep_grains()` and are only meaningful in tables grouped by it.
    ;;
  }

  block t_prog: TextBlock {
    content: @md
## Programmatic test

Six Programmatic ad ids selected at once. In `stg_campaigns` and `creative_city_mapping` these rows have a **null campaign_id**, so the v2 bridge join had to be made null-safe for them to get a network scope at all. The flight window is the min/max envelope across all six ads. The block condition is `filter_model.report_filter in attention_base.report_filter` (no empty-control fallback on this tab).
    ;;
  }

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Tab 1 blocks (Direct 10605)
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  block v_summary: VizBlock {
    label: 'Campaign level'
    viz: DataTable {
      dataset: attention
      filter {
        field: r(attention_base.is_in_flight_range)
        operator: 'is'
        value: true
      }
      conditions: [
        "filter_model.report_filter == coalesce((attention_base.report_filter | first()), '__all__') or coalesce((attention_base.report_filter | first()), '__all__') == '__all__'"
      ]
      fields: [
        VizFieldFull {
          ref: r(attention.campaign_datapoints)
          format {
            type: 'number'
            pattern: 'inherited'
          }
        },
        VizFieldFull {
          ref: r(attention.attention_seconds_average)
          format {
            type: 'number'
            pattern: 'inherited'
          }
        },
        VizFieldFull {
          ref: r(attention.campaign_average_attention_seconds)
          format {
            type: 'number'
            pattern: 'inherited'
          }
        },
        VizFieldFull {
          ref: r(attention.average_attention_seconds)
          format {
            type: 'number'
            pattern: 'inherited'
          }
        },
        VizFieldFull {
          ref: r(attention.network_average_overall)
          format {
            type: 'number'
            pattern: 'inherited'
          }
        },
        VizFieldFull {
          ref: r(attention.attention_events)
          format {
            type: 'number'
            pattern: 'inherited'
          }
        },
        VizFieldFull {
          ref: r(attention.attention_vs_campaign)
          format {
            type: 'number'
            pattern: 'inherited'
          }
        },
        VizFieldFull {
          ref: r(attention.attention_vs_network)
          format {
            type: 'number'
            pattern: 'inherited'
          }
        },
        VizFieldFull {
          ref: r(attention.selected_campaign_start_date)
          format {
            type: 'date'
          }
        },
        VizFieldFull {
          ref: r(attention.selected_campaign_end_date)
          format {
            type: 'date'
          }
        }
      ]
      settings {
        show_row_number: true
        row_limit: 5000
        aggregate_awareness {
          enabled: true
          debug_comments: true
        }
      }
    }
  }

  block v_gender: VizBlock {
    label: 'By gender (network benchmark per gender)'
